status prints the daemon's pid, version and socket when it answers, and
exits 3 with the command to start it when it does not. Scripts can use the
exit code alone.

Usage:
  ley daemon status [flags]

Examples:
  ley daemon status
  ley daemon status --json # a DaemonInfo message; only socketPath when not running

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for status

Global Flags:
      --bin string      path to the leylined binary
      --json            machine output: proto3 JSON (NDJSON for streams)
      --log string      daemon log file (default: ~/Library/Logs/Leyline/leylined.log)
      --socket string   daemon socket path (default: user daemon UDS, $LEYLINE_SOCKET)
